---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
export const articles={ 'how-to-select-ball-valve':{title:'How to Select an Industrial Ball Valve',body:'Ball valve selection must account for media properties, design pressure, operating temperature, size, end connection, and automation requirements. First identify whether the media is corrosive, abrasive, or solids-bearing, then select compatible body, ball, and seat materials.'}, 'floating-vs-trunnion':{title:'Floating vs. Trunnion-Mounted Ball Valves',body:'A floating ball valve uses line pressure to push the ball against the downstream seat, providing a compact design. A trunnion-mounted ball valve supports the ball through upper and lower stems, making it suitable for larger sizes and higher pressure.'}, 'fugitive-emissions':{title:'Fugitive Emissions: Controlling Invisible Leakage',body:'Low-emissions performance relies on the stem packing system, surface finish, assembly preload, and cycle testing. Specify the required test standard and cycle count early in the project specification.'} };
export function getStaticPaths(){return Object.entries(articles).map(([slug,article])=>({params:{slug},props:{article}}));} const {article}=Astro.props;
---
<BaseLayout title={`${article.title} | BallValve`}><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><Breadcrumb current="Technical Blog" /><p class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL NOTE</p><h1 class="title">{article.title}</h1></div></section><article class="section container prose"><p>{article.body}</p><h2>Engineering guidance</h2><p>Before the final model is selected, an applications engineer should review the full piping conditions, control logic, and project specifications. A standard product is only the starting point; the right match is what delivers reliable operation.</p></article></BaseLayout>
